  "goodToKnow": "Belangen means to take legal action against someone or hold them liable: strafrechtlich belangt werden (to be prosecuted). It's mostly used in the passive and in legal or news contexts. Der Belang is a matter of concern: von Belang sein (to be relevant), die Belange der Bürger (the concerns of citizens). Belanglos means trivial: belangloses Gerede (small talk). Was mich anbelangt, from the related verb anbelangen, means as far as I'm concerned."
